# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
mutation.json

# make build output
/bin/

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file. go.work itself is committed on purpose - see the comment
# inside it and docs/architecture/adr-0001-module-layout.md - but its checksum
# file is generated and machine-local.
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Local working notes, not meant to be committed.
NOTES.md

# Claude Code. .claude/settings.json IS committed - it carries the project's
# shared permission allowlist, derived from the Makefile targets. Anything
# personal or machine-specific belongs in settings.local.json instead, so that
# absolute paths and one-off approvals never reach the repository.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
